Lab 5: Install and Customize RHACM Observability Stack
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Install and configure Prometheus for cluster monitoring and metrics collection • Deploy and customize Grafana dashboards for visualizing cluster performance data • Set up Alertmanager for real-time monitoring alerts and notifications • Integrate the complete observability stack with Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM) • Configure monitoring across multiple OpenShift clusters • Create custom monitoring rules and alert policies

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of Kubernetes and OpenShift concepts • Familiarity with YAML configuration files • Knowledge of Linux command-line operations • Understanding of monitoring and observability concepts • Access to OpenShift cluster with cluster-admin privileges • Basic knowledge of Prometheus query language (PromQL)

Lab Environment Setup
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with OpenShift clusters already deployed. Simply click Start Lab to access your environment - no need to build your own VM or install OpenShift from scratch.

Your lab environment includes: • OpenShift 4.12+ cluster with RHACM installed • Command-line tools (oc, kubectl, helm) • Internet connectivity for downloading required components • Sufficient resources for monitoring stack deployment

Task 1: Install Prometheus for Cluster Monitoring
Subtask 1.1: Verify RHACM Installation and Create Monitoring Namespace
First, let's verify that RHACM is properly installed and create a dedicated namespace for our observability stack.

Connect to your OpenShift cluster:
# Verify cluster connection
oc whoami
oc cluster-info
Check RHACM installation status:
# Verify RHACM operator is installed
oc get operators -A | grep advanced-cluster-management

# Check RHACM MultiClusterHub status
oc get multiclusterhub -A
Create monitoring namespace:
# Create dedicated namespace for observability
oc create namespace rhacm-observability

# Verify namespace creation
oc get namespace rhacm-observability
Subtask 1.2: Install Prometheus Operator
Create Prometheus Operator subscription:
# Create the subscription file
cat << 'EOF' > prometheus-operator-subscription.yaml
apiVersion: operators.coreos.com/v1alpha1
kind: Subscription
metadata:
  name: prometheus-operator
  namespace: rhacm-observability
spec:
  channel: beta
  name: prometheus-operator
  source: community-operators
  sourceNamespace: openshift-marketplace
  installPlanApproval: Automatic
EOF

# Apply the subscription
oc apply -f prometheus-operator-subscription.yaml
Wait for operator installation:
# Check operator installation status
oc get csv -n rhacm-observability

# Wait for the operator to be ready (this may take 2-3 minutes)
oc wait --for=condition=Succeeded csv -l operators.coreos.com/prometheus-operator.rhacm-observability -n rhacm-observability --timeout=300s
Subtask 1.3: Deploy Prometheus Instance
Create Prometheus configuration:
cat << 'EOF' > prometheus-instance.yaml
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: Prometheus
metadata:
  name: rhacm-prometheus
  namespace: rhacm-observability
  labels:
    app: rhacm-prometheus
spec:
  replicas: 1
  retention: 30d
  storage:
    volumeClaimTemplate:
      spec:
        accessModes:
        - ReadWriteOnce
        resources:
          requests:
            storage: 10Gi
  serviceAccountName: prometheus-rhacm
  serviceMonitorSelector:
    matchLabels:
      team: rhacm
  ruleSelector:
    matchLabels:
      team: rhacm
  resources:
    requests:
      memory: 400Mi
      cpu: 100m
    limits:
      memory: 2Gi
      cpu: 1000m
  securityContext:
    runAsNonRoot: true
    runAsUser: 65534
EOF

# Apply Prometheus configuration
oc apply -f prometheus-instance.yaml
Create ServiceAccount and RBAC:
cat << 'EOF' > prometheus-rbac.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: prometheus-rhacm
  namespace: rhacm-observability
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: prometheus-rhacm
rules:
- apiGroups: [""]
  resources:
  - nodes
  - nodes/proxy
  - services
  - endpoints
  - pods
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
- apiGroups:
  - extensions
  resources:
  - ingresses
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
- nonResourceURLs: ["/metrics"]
  verbs: ["get"]
---
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRoleBinding
metadata:
  name: prometheus-rhacm
roleRef:
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io
  kind: ClusterRole
  name: prometheus-rhacm
subjects:
- kind: ServiceAccount
  name: prometheus-rhacm
  namespace: rhacm-observability
EOF

# Apply RBAC configuration
oc apply -f prometheus-rbac.yaml
Verify Prometheus deployment:
# Check Prometheus pod status
oc get pods -n rhacm-observability -l app.kubernetes.io/name=prometheus

# Check Prometheus service
oc get svc -n rhacm-observability -l app.kubernetes.io/name=prometheus
